# Lab manager (#155): one lab Pi per line. Copy to /etc/lab-manager/pis.conf on the Pi 5.
# Keep the real file local: it isn't committed (it holds the Pis' MACs, MASTERPLAN §3.5).
#
#   NAME MAC[,MAC] the address comes from the router's DHCP leases (/tmp/dhcp.leases), so
#                  it follows the Pi when DHCP gives it a new one; the newest lease of its
#                  MACs wins. List both of the hub's MACs: its random, stable one (while
#                  UNKNOWN_DEVICE is on) and its real one (when that is fixed).
#   NAME ADDRESS   a fixed IP, for a Pi with a static lease
pi2 e4:5f:01:00:00:01
pi3 e6:14:f0:00:00:03,dc:a6:32:00:00:03
pi4 e4:5f:01:00:00:02
